'''Pahlavani''' is an extinct variety of [[Persian language|Persian]] that was spoken in the [[Chakhansur District]], in the [[Nimruz Province]] of [[Afghanistan]]. It was reportedly an unwritten language that is believed to be similar to [[Dari]].<ref>{{e22|phv|Pahlavani}}</ref>

